            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "glad to be using mini plugin :) \r\n\r\nyeah, nothing fancy in my setup, here are some commands to reproduce: \r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim     # open a new nvim process\r\n:e test1.txt     # open a random file\r\n:tabnew test2.txt   # another random file \r\n:tabnew test3.txt.  # another one \r\n:q!        # quit test3.txt\r\n```\r\n\r\nAt this point, the tabline shows three files `test1.txt, test2.txt, test3.txt` \r\nBut there are only two files I am working with",
